  newspaperHeadlines:
  - Grieving a Hero
  - Local Hero Dead
  - Queer Death of a Businessman
  AllNewspaperPieces:
  - possibly leapt from the roof of the building.
  - apparently fallen from a great height.
  - possibly been thrown from an upper floor.
  - a revered NYPD investigator,
  - a well-intentioned NYPD investigator,
  - a rookie investigator for the NYPD,
  - is committed to solving the case and finding justice for our departed hero.
  - also asks the public to come forward with any information that may be relevant
    to the case.
  - "also hinted that Robert\u2019s personal life might not have been as wholesome
    as it appeared."
  - "was five months pregnant at the time of his death.\r"
  - "is deeply upset by his sudden passing.\r"
  - "is hysterical with grief for her departed father.\r"
  - "tepidly supported\r"
  - "overflowed with praise for\r"
  - "clung to the quality of\r"
  - "his life choices,\r"
  - "his character and disposition,\r"
  - the man she thought she knew,
  - "wasn\u2019t nearly so forgiving.\r"
  - "didn\u2019t have such a straightforward opinion.\r"
  - "wasn\u2019t nearly so coherent.\r"
  - "Having grown distant from his father since the divorce,\r"
  - "Privy to a side of him that the public never saw,\r\r"
  - "Although they hadn\u2019t spoken for quite some time,"
  - "had a complicated relationship with Mr. Evergreen. Tragically, any hope of making
    peace died with Jim\u2019s father on Monday morning.\r"
  - "had a strained relationship with Mr. Evergreen. As a child, however, Jim\u2019s
    idolized his father, and it\u2019s clear that he still feels such admiration
    today."
  - "deeply resents Mr. Evergreen, believing him to be responsible for his parents\u2019
    divorce and for much of Jim\u2019s own suffering.\r"
  - "business partner Ms. Max\r"
  - "business partner Ms. Maxine\r"
  - "subordinate Ms. Maxine\r"
  - "a woman confidently navigating the male-dominated world of business,\r"
  - a straight-laced woman with a keen eye for business,
  - "\ra ruthless businesswoman with a steely disposition,\r"
  - "declined to speak about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s personal life, only describing
    him as an excellent boss and business partner.\r"
  - "described Mr. Evergreen as a consummate professional and an excellent boss and
    business partner.\r"
  - "refused to speak directly about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s personal life, but clearly
    knew more than she was willing to admit.\r"
  - "At the time of his death, Mr. Evergreen was in a relationship with a member
    of the US navy. His partner, who will remain anonymous for his own safety,\r"
  - "Mr. Evergreen will be missed by the community, having built a vast network of
    friends throughout his life. One such friend, Lt. Michael Bailey of the US navy,\r"
  - "Perhaps Mr. Evergreen\u2019s best-kept secret was Lt. Michael Bailey, his lover
    of fifteen years, known only to his closest friends and family. Lt Bailey\r"
  - "suffers under the military\u2019s anti-gay atmosphere. For him, Mr. Evergreen
    was a much-needed reprieve.\r"
  - "is a devoted and well-respected naval officer.\r"
  - "is a gay sailor with many years\u2019 experience under his belt.\r"
  - Despite his deep and long-lasting relationship with Mr. Evergreen,
  - "As one of Mr. Evergreen\u2019s closest companions,\r"
  - "Despite claiming to regret his relationship with Mr. Evergreen,\r"
  AllParaPieces:
  - 'Robert Evergreen was found dead outside his workplace Monday morning, having '
  - Mr. Evergreen was the founder and CEO of Abundantia Investments, a father of
    two, and a well-liked community member. According to Detective Novak, the investigation
    is still ongoing. Novak,
  - "Evergreen is survived by two children, Jim Evergreen and Julia Anderson, as
    well as an ex-wife. Mr. Evergreen\u2019s daughter Julia\r"
  - 'Although Julia '
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s son, Jim,  "
  - Jim
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s ex-wife declined to comment for this article."
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s company will remain in operation, led by his "
  - Elliot. Ms. Elliot,
  - "when reached for comment he simply said: \u201CWe were unable to spend as much
    time together as I wish we could have.\u201D"
  MuckrakerArticlePieces:
  - "Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and self-made businessman, was found dead outside
    his workplace Monday morning, having possibly leapt from an upper floor. Mr.
    Evergreen was the CEO of Abundantia Investments, a father of two, and a friend
    to many. He was also a closeted gay man in a secret relationship with a US service
    member.\r"
  - "Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and self-made businessman, was found dead outside
    his workplace Monday morning, having apparently fallen from a great height. Mr.
    Evergreen was the CEO of Abundantia Investments, a father of two, and a friend
    to many. He was also a closeted gay man in a secret relationship with a US service
    member.\r"
  - 'Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and self-made businessman, was found dead outside
    his workplace Monday morning, having possibly been thrown from an upper floor.
    Mr. Evergreen was the CEO of Abundantia Investments, a father of two, and a friend
    to many. He was also a closeted gay man in a secret relationship with a US service
    member.

'
  - "Mr. Evergreen is survived by two children, Julia Anderson and Jim Evergreen.
    Mr Evergreen divorced his wife five years ago. She declined to comment for this
    article. His daughter, Julia, is wounded by his death. Despite taking a neutral
    stance toward him when interviewed, it\u2019s clear that Julia loved him in life.\r"
  - 'Mr. Evergreen is survived by two children, Julia Anderson and Jim Evergreen.
    Mr Evergreen divorced his wife five years ago. She declined to comment for this
    article. His daughter, Julia, is deeply wounded by his untimely death. She is
    a devoted, loving daughter who held her father in the highest regard.

'
  - 'Mr. Evergreen is survived by two children, Julia Anderson and Jim Evergreen.
    Mr Evergreen divorced his wife five years ago. She declined to comment for this
    article. His daughter, Julia, loved her feather dearly. However, she is clearly
    in denial about his true nature: that of a distant, uncaring parent.

'
  - "Jim, on the other hand, had a much more complicated feelings about Mr. Evergreen.
    Jim didn\u2019t take his parents\u2019 divorce well, and when he discovered his
    father\u2019s homosexuality, their relationship only became more precarious.\r"
  - "Jim didn\u2019t take his parent\u2019s divorce well, and struggled to accept
    his father\u2019s homosexuality. But despite these difficulties, it\u2019s clear
    that Jim had a deep love for him. \u201COur father was Jim\u2019s hero,\u201D
    said Julia.\r\n"
  - "Jim had little love for his father. He grew resentful toward Mr. Evergreen after
    the divorce, and when he discovered his father\u2019s homosexuality, this hatred
    deepened. \u201CHe was so flustered,\u201D explained Julia, \u201Cso angry.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Rumors about Mr. Evergreen were abound in his workplace. His friend and business
    partner, Max Elliot, didn\u2019t discuss his homosexuality. However, it\u2019s
    clear she felt a sense of kinship toward him. \u201CThis is a tough world to
    be in if you aren\u2019t part of the boys\u2019 club,\u201D Max said when asked
    about Mr. Evergreen. \u201CRobert was never anything but professional with me\u2026
    it\u2019s only right that I do the same for him now.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Rumors about Mr. Evergreen were abound in his workplace. His business partner,
    Max Elliot, didn\u2019t discuss his homosexuality. However, it\u2019s clear that
    she felt a sense of kinship toward him. \u201CThis is a tough world to be in
    if you aren\u2019t part of the boys\u2019 club,\u201D Max said when asked about
    Mr. Evergreen. \u201CRobert was never anything but professional with me\u2026
    it\u2019s only right that I do the same for him now.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Rumors about Mr. Evergreen were abound in his workplace. His subordinate, Max
    Elliot, didn\u2019t discuss his homosexuality. However, it\u2019s clear that
    she felt a sense of kinship toward him. \u201CThis is a tough world to be in
    if you aren\u2019t part of the boys\u2019 club,\u201D Max said when asked about
    Mr. Evergreen. \u201CRobert was never anything but professional with me\u2026
    it\u2019s only right that I do the same for him now.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen was in a covert relationship with a career sailor in the US navy.
    The Local Rag is unable to name him here without putting his profession and his
    safety at risk. When asked about the consequences he might face if his homosexuality
    were exposed, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s partner gave a simple yet damning response:
    \u201CIf my superior officers find out, I will be discharged.\u201D Unable to
    grieve Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death publicly, his partner will have no choice but
    to mourn in private, as he continues his silent struggle against the US military\u2019s
    rampant homophobia.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen was in a long-term relationship with a career sailor in the US
    navy, but the Local Rag cannot name him here without putting his profession and
    his safety at risk. When asked about the consequences Mr. Evergreen\u2019s partner
    might face if his homosexuality were exposed, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s friend Lt.
    Michael Bailey gave a simple yet damning response: \u201CHe will be discharged.\u201D
    Unable to grieve Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death publicly, his partner will have no
    choice but to mourn in private, as he continues his silent struggle against the
    US military\u2019s rampant homophobia.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen was in a long-term relationship with Lt. Michael Bailey, a US
    naval officer. By revealing himself as Mr. Evergreen\u2019s partner, Lt. Bailey
    is putting his profession and his safety at risk. When asked about the consequences
    he might face if his homosexuality were exposed, Lt. Bailey gave a simple yet
    damning response: \u201CIf my superior officers find out, I will be discharged.\u201D
    Unable to grieve Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death publicly, Lt. Bailey will have no
    choice but to mourn in private, as he continues his silent struggle against the
    US military\u2019s rampant homophobia.\r\n"
  SQArticlePieces:
  - "Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and businessman, was found dead Monday morning
    outside of his workplace, having apparently fallen from a great height. Mr. Evergreen
    was a well-liked member of our community and the founder of Abundantia Investments.
    Detective Novak of the NYPD stated that \u201CThe department does not, at this
    time, wish to speculate on the specific manner of the death, whether it was accident,
    murder, or suicide, as the investigation is still ongoing.\u201D Novak, a revered
    NYPD investigator, encourages the public to come forward with any information
    about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death."
  - "Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and businessman, was found dead Monday morning
    outside of his workplace, having apparently fallen from a great height. Mr. Evergreen
    was a well-liked member of our community and the founder of Abundantia Investments.
    Detective Novak of the NYPD stated that \u201CThe department does not, at this
    time, wish to speculate on the specific manner of the death, whether it was accident,
    murder, or suicide, as the investigation is still ongoing.\u201D Novak encourages
    the public to come forward with any information about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death."
  - "Mr. Robert Evergreen, local hero and businessman, was found dead Monday morning
    outside of his workplace, having apparently fallen from a great height. Mr. Evergreen
    was a well-liked member of our community and the founder of Abundantia Investments.
    Detective Novak of the NYPD stated that \u201CThe department does not, at this
    time, wish to speculate on the specific manner of the death, whether it was accident,
    murder, or suicide, as the investigation is still ongoing.\u201D Novak, a rookie
    NYPD investigator, encourages the public to come forward with any information
    about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s death."
  - "Mr. Evergreen is survived by his ex-wife and his two children, Julia Anderson
    and Jim Evergreen. When reached for comment, both children expressed grief at
    the sudden loss of their father. Julia, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s daughter, was five
    months pregnant at the time of his death. \u201CI wanted my child to meet him,\u201D
    she said. \u201CBut now that will never happen.\u201D\r"
  - "Mr. Evergreen is survived by his ex-wife and his two children, Julia Anderson
    and Jim Evergreen. When reached for comment, both children expressed grief at
    the sudden loss of their father. Julia, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s daughter is deeply
    upset by his death, having cherished him dearly in life. \u201CMy father was
    a happy, successful man,\u201D she said. \u201CHe loved his family.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen is survived by his ex-wife and his two children, Julia Anderson
    and Jim Evergreen. When reached for comment, both children expressed grief at
    the sudden loss of their father. Julia, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s daughter, was overcome
    with emotion when interviewed about his death. \u201CMy father was a happy, successful
    man,\u201D she said. \u201CHe loved his family.\u201D \r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s son, Jim, was especially close with him as a child. Even
    after starting his own life, Jim made every effort to stay in touch with his
    father. \u201CI knew him better than anybody,\u201D Jim said when asked about
    their relationship.\r"
  - "On the other hand, Mr. Evergreen\u2019s relationship with his son Jim was far
    from perfect. Despite these difficulties, however, it\u2019s clear that the two
    of them were very close. \u201CI knew him better than anybody,\u201D Jim said
    when asked about his father.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen and his son Jim, on the other hand, were never especially close.
    Despite this difficulty, however, it\u2019s clear that Jim\u2019s father held
    great importance to him. \u201CYou have to understand,\u201D Julia said, \u201Cour
    father was Jim\u2019s hero. Always had been.\u201D\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen built his company, Abundantia Investments, from the ground up.
    For now, the company will be led by Mr. Evergreen\u2019s friend and associate,
    Ms. Max Elliot, who described Mr. Evergreen as a consummate professional and
    an excellent boss and business partner.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen built his company, Abundantia Investments, from the ground up.
    For now, the company will be led by Mr. Evergreen\u2019s associate, Ms. Max Elliot,
    who described Mr. Evergreen as a consummate professional and an excellent boss
    and business partner.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen built his company, Abundantia Investments, from the ground up.
    For now, the company will be led by Mr. Evergreen\u2019s subordinate, Ms. Max
    Elliot, who described Mr. Evergreen as a consummate professional and an excellent
    boss and business partner.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen was in a romantic relationship at the time of his death. The Local
    Rag is unable to name his partner here without putting his career as a US naval
    sailor at risk. However, he is deeply disturbed by Mr. Evergreen\u2019s sudden
    passing. \u201CWe were unable to spend as much time together as I wish we could\u2019ve,\u201D
    he said when reached for comment.\r\n"
  - "In addition to his family, Mr. Evergreen leaves behind a vast network of friends.
    One of his closest friends, Lieutenant Michael Bailey of the US Navy, reached
    out to the Local Rag to express his deep remorse at Mr. Evergreen\u2019s passing.
    \u201CWe were unable to spend as much time together as I wish we could\u2019ve,\u201D
    Lt. Bailey said when asked about their relationship.\r\n"
  - "At the time of his death, Mr. Evergreen was in a long-term romantic relationship
    with Lieutenant Michael Bailey of the United States Navy. Lt. Bailey is deeply
    disturbed by the sudden and unexpected nature of Mr. Evergreen\u2019s passing.
    \u201CWe were unable to spend as much time together as I wish we could\u2019ve,\u201D
    he said of his and Mr. Evergreen\u2019s relationship when reached for comment.\r\n"
  TabloidArticlePieces:
  - "Robert Evergreen, CEO of Abundantia Investments, was found dead under mysterious
    circumstances on Monday morning, having apparently jumped from the roof of his
    office building. While he was known as a family man and an upstanding citizen
    of our city, there was a shocking secret hiding in his closet - Robert Evergreen
    was a homosexual.\r"
  - 'Robert Evergreen, CEO of Abundantia Investments, was found dead under mysterious
    circumstances on Monday morning, having fallen from the roof of his office building.
    While he was known as a family man and an upstanding citizen of our city, there
    was a shocking secret hiding in his closet - Robert Evergreen was a homosexual.

'
  - "Robert Evergreen, CEO of Abundantia Investments, was found dead under mysterious
    circumstances on Monday morning, having apparently been pushed from the roof
    of his office building. While he was known as a family man and an upstanding
    citizen of our city, there was a shocking secret hiding in his closet - Robert
    Evergreen was a homosexual. \r\n"
  - 'Mr. Evergreen leaves behind an ex-wife and two children, each of whom held a
    conflicting opinion of his deviant lifestyle. When asked for comment, his daughter
    Julia Anderson staunchly defended his homosexuality, making her approval of his
    lifestyle very clear. His son Jim Evergreen, on the other hand, held no such
    perspective.

'
  - "Mr. Evergreen leaves behind an ex-wife and two children, each of whom was left
    damaged by his deviant lifestyle. When asked for comment, his daughter Julia
    Anderson asked not to discuss his homosexuality. She instead redirected the conversation
    toward his business and his family life. Mr. Evergreen\u2019s son Jim Evergreen,
    however, had no such request.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen leaves behind an ex-wife and two children, each of whom was left
    damaged by his deviant lifestyle. When asked to comment on her father\u2019s
    sexual orientation, his daughter Julia Anderson reacted poorly and with strongly
    worded reproach. His son Jim Evergreen, on the other hand, had no such reservations.\r"
  - "Jim expressed bitterness towards his father in both life and death, describing
    Mr. Evergreen as a neglectful and callous parent \u2013 an attitude that only
    worsened post-divorce as he freely pursued his homosexuality Mr. Evergreen\u2019s
    ex-wife declined to comment for this article.\r\n"
  - "Jim is deep in the throes of grief after his father\u2019s death, but admitted
    that Mr. Evergreen was a neglectful and uncaring parent \u2013 an attitude that
    only worsened post-divorce as he freely pursued his homosexuality. Mr. Evergreen\u2019s
    ex-wife declined to comment for this article.\r\n"
  - "Jim seemed to be on the verge of tears as he described his father\u2019s cruel
    and callous nature. Apparently, this attitude only worsened post-divorce as Mr.
    Evergreen freely pursued his homosexual preferences. Mr. Evergreen\u2019s ex-wife
    declined to comment for this article.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s company will remain in operation, headed by Ms. Maxine
    Elliot, a confident woman with a firm grip on the male-dominated world of business.
    She wouldn\u2019t outright confirm nor deny any allegations, but it\u2019s clear
    that Mr. Evergreen\u2019s sex life was something of an open secret at his company.
    \u201CThere was the occasional business trip or social gathering where he\u2019d
    quietly slip out and we wouldn\u2019t see him again until morning,\u201D she
    explained.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s company will remain in operation, led by Ms. Maxine Elliot,
    a straight-laced woman with a sharp eye for business. She wouldn\u2019t outright
    confirm nor deny anything about Mr. Evergreen\u2019s sex life, but it\u2019s
    clear that the details were something of an open secret at his company. \u201CThere
    was the occasional business trip or social gathering where he\u2019d quietly
    slip out and we wouldn\u2019t see him again until morning,\u201D she explained.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s business will remain in operation, left in the cold and
    steely hands of a ruthless businesswoman named Ms. Maxine Elliot. She wouldn\u2019t
    outright confirm nor deny any allegations, but it\u2019s clear that Mr. Evergreen\u2019s
    sex life was something of an open secret at his company. \u201CThere was the
    occasional business trip or social gathering where he\u2019d quietly slip out
    and we wouldn\u2019t see him again until morning,\u201D she explained.\r\n"
  - "Mr. Evergreen\u2019s mysterious lover, a sailor for the US Navy, asked to remain
    anonymous for his own personal safety. He and Mr. Evergreen had been in an on-and-off
    relationship for the past fifteen years, beginning when Mr. Evergreen was still
    married to his ex-wife. While he refused to elaborate on Mr. Evergreen\u2019s
    marriage or the scandalous details of his and Mr. Evergreen\u2019s relationship,
    he did admit that he ultimately came to \u201Cregret\u201D his relationship with
    the businessman.\r\n"
  - "The details of Mr. Evergreen\u2019s relationship are a well-kept secret. Mr.
    Evergreen\u2019s longtime friend and confidant Lieutenant Michael Bailey, however,
    was more than willing to spill the beans. According to Lt. Bailey, Mr. Evergreen
    had been seeing a US Naval sailor for the past fifteen years, beginning when
    Mr. Evergreen was still married to his ex-wife. While he wouldn\u2019t elaborate
    on the details, Lt. Bailey did admit that the sailor came to \u201Cregret\u201D
    his relationship with the businessman.\r\n"
  - "As for Mr. Evergreen\u2019s lover? That would be one Lieutenant Michael Bailey
    of the United States Navy, a strapping, mature sailor with a rich southern accent.
    Lt. Bailey had been in an on-and-off relationship with Mr. Evergreen for the
    past fifteen years, beginning when Mr. Evergreen was still married to his ex-wife.
    While he would not elaborate on the details when asked, Lt. Bailey did admit
    that he ultimately came to \u201Cregret\u201D his relationship with the businessman.
    \r\n"
